{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Gift would be my pick if it is the Christmas album I recognize, because it connects directly to the holiday albums I repeatedly returned to.",
    "Lead With Your Heart, Someone To Watch Over Me and Forte appeal to my interest in vocals, familiar standards and harmony, which feels connected to my listening to The New Old Fashioned."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "In The Lonely Hour and the Fifty Shades Of Grey soundtrack give me little reason to expect the holiday mood or harmony-focused listening I want right now.",
    "The Greatest Hits Collection, Box Set, Storm and The Life Of A Song do not give me enough recognizable musical connection to justify trying them during a visit when I would choose only one album."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "An album having vocals is too broad a connection for me; the holiday mood, familiar songs and vocal harmonies are what make particular albums appealing.",
    "A collection sounding familiar or comprehensive does not make it a match unless I recognize the artist or know which songs it contains."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Several holiday albums in my history, including repeated listening to The Classic Christmas Album, make a recognizable Christmas connection especially meaningful to me.",
    "My interest in The New Old Fashioned makes harmony-focused albums plausible choices, but that interest does not mean I am ready to explore any vocal album or choose several at once."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in holiday music and vocal harmony, but stretched that interest to albums with too little recognizable connection to what I want now."
}"}
